<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc/mapping/000> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "The cleanest element-level row. Residual gap: IFC splits curtain walling into IfcCurtainWall while EF_25_10 classifies the wall function regardless of construction." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.85 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcWall ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcWall" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:closeMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id uniclass:EF_25_10 ;
    sssom:subject_label "Walls" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc/mapping/001> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "Direct at the element level. IfcRoof is frequently a container aggregating slabs and beams; the EF code classifies the whole either way." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.85 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcRoof ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcRoof" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:closeMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id uniclass:EF_30_10 ;
    sssom:subject_label "Roofs" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc/mapping/002> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "Crossed scopes rather than a clean match: IfcSlab is broader (it also serves as roof slab and landing, with a predefined type discriminating) and narrower (a floor element includes build-up beyond the structural slab). Kept at closeMatch because in exchange practice floor elements land as IfcSlab." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.7 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcSlab ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcSlab" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:closeMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id uniclass:EF_30_20 ;
    sssom:subject_label "Floors" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc/mapping/003> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "Decks (including bridge decks) have no dedicated IFC4 class; they are modelled as slabs by convention. Related, not close: IFC4 predates the infrastructure entities that would carry this properly." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.6 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcSlab ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcSlab" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:relatedMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id uniclass:EF_30_30 ;
    sssom:subject_label "Decks" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc/mapping/004> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "Direct at the element level: both classify the door as an installed filling of an opening, and neither side splits doorsets from doors at this depth." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.9 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcDoor ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcDoor" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:closeMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id uniclass:EF_25_30_25 ;
    sssom:subject_label "Doors" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc/mapping/005> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "Direct at the element level, same shape as the doors row; IFC's IfcWindow likewise covers the window as installed opening filling." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.9 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcWindow ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcWindow" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:closeMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id uniclass:EF_25_30_97 ;
    sssom:subject_label "Windows" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc/mapping/006> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "Direct at the element level: IfcStair, like the EF code, denotes the whole vertical-circulation element and aggregates flights and landings beneath it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.9 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcStair ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcStair" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:closeMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id uniclass:EF_35_10 ;
    sssom:subject_label "Stairs" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc/mapping/007> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "Direct at the element level, mirroring the stairs row: IfcRamp aggregates ramp flights exactly as IfcStair aggregates stair flights." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.9 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcRamp ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcRamp" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:closeMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id uniclass:EF_35_20 ;
    sssom:subject_label "Ramps" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc/mapping/008> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "Foundations is the broader function: IfcFooting carries the shallow-foundation case. Read as 'IfcFooting is the narrower concept'." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.8 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcFooting ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcFooting" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:narrowMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id uniclass:EF_20_05_30 ;
    sssom:subject_label "Foundations" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc/mapping/009> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "The deep-foundation case of the row above. IFC splits by construction method what Uniclass unifies by function; neither is wrong, and the crosswalk must carry both rows or silently lose piles." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.8 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcPile ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcPile" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:narrowMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id uniclass:EF_20_05_30 ;
    sssom:subject_label "Foundations" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc/mapping/010> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "IFC4 has no IfcCeiling class at all: ceilings are IfcCovering occurrences discriminated only by a CEILING predefined type. IfcCovering is the broader concept (it also carries claddings, floor coverings and wrappings), so this is a broadMatch with real information loss at the class level." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.8 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcCovering ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcCovering" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:broadMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id uniclass:EF_30_25_12 ;
    sssom:subject_label "Ceilings" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc/mapping/011> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "The stratification mismatch made explicit: Uniclass separates the wall element (EF_25_10) from the wall system (Ss_25), while a single IfcWall occurrence answers for both readings. One IFC class, two Uniclass strata. Any tool that maps IfcWall to exactly one Uniclass table has already made an undeclared modelling decision." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.6 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcWall ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcWall" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:relatedMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id uniclass:Ss_25 ;
    sssom:subject_label "Wall and barrier systems" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc/mapping/012> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "System-stratum counterpart of the EF door row; same conflation as Ss_25." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.55 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc> ;
    sssom:object_id ifc:IfcDoor ;
    sssom:object_label "IfcDoor" ;
    sssom:predicate_id skos:relatedMatch ;
    sssom:subject_id uniclass:Ss_25_30 ;
    sssom:subject_label "Door and window systems" .

<https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc/mapping/013> a sssom:Mapping ;
    rdfs:comment "System-stratum counterpart of the EF window row." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo orcid:0009-0001-7244-794X ;
    sssom:confidence 0.55 ;
    sssom:mapping_justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/construction-crosswalks/uniclass-ifc> ;
